prebuilt/torch2.7.1-cu126-cp311-cxx11abi1/fast_layer_norm_cuda_v2_cs.so is OpenDDE 1.1.1's fused-LayerNorm extension
(opendde/model/layer_norm/kernel/: layer_norm_cuda.cpp, layer_norm_cuda_kernel.cu, compat.h, type_shim.h; in this tree under
opendde/stock/src/opendde/model/layer_norm/kernel/) compiled for sm_80 and sm_90 against PyTorch's C++ extension headers and the CUDA toolkit.
layer_norm_cuda.cpp, compat.h and type_shim.h are compiled unmodified. layer_norm_cuda_kernel.cu is compiled with one change made by this
package: each of its 25 kernel-launch statements that name no CUDA stream is given the current stream (`<<<grid, block>>>` becomes
`<<<grid, block, 0, at::cuda::getCurrentCUDAStream().stream()>>>`); device code, every other statement and the file's own notices are unchanged.
src/layer_norm_cuda_kernel.cu is that modified file exactly as compiled; opendde/opt/opendde_opt/lnstream.py (to_current_stream) makes the change
and `python -m opendde_opt.lnstream prebuild` rebuilds the binary from the four sources.

